    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0507" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157Sa29/3</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the British Ambassador on Special Mission</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reading</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to refer to this
                    Government’s note No. 262 of February 24, 1914,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d420-f1"/>
                    suggesting that the Government of the United States and the Government of Canada
                    should refer to the International Joint Commission for investigation and report
                    certain questions outlined in the note regarding the development and use of the
                    waters forming the boundary between the United States and Canada, and to inquire
                    whether the Canadian Government is now ready to submit the matter to the
                    Commission and if not, whether it is willing to join with this Government in
                    submitting to the Commission for investigation and report the matter referred to
                    in Section 9 of the Act of Congress approved March 2, 1919, a copy of which was
                    transmitted to your Embassy in the Department’s note of March 31 last.<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d420-f2"/></p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d420-f1" n="20" xml:id="d420-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; no answer to this note was ever received.</p>
